ugandan opposition politician kisa  beside is used to being arrested  for more than 20 years he's demonstrated  against the government of president  yoweri museveni and challenged him in  four elections his protest on monday was  against the rising cost of living  at the fuel pumps prices have gone up 70  percent in the last year  food prices are climbing too  motorbike taxi riders are among millions  whose livelihoods are affected  what used to be five dollars a while ago  is now fourteen dollars they should  reduce the price of fuel  president museveni has ruled uganda ever  since he led a rebellion and took power  by force in 1986 he's rejected some of  the ideas to bring down prices removing  taxes  or subsidizing many of the imports is  suicidal  and a blunder  how then we fund our budget for the  roads  electricity schools  medicine  security atc  beside who also protested last week says  it's corruption rather than public  spending that's draining government  coffers  arrest those who have taken our money  the thieves they are known return their  property so that it serves the people  who are in crisis if we are able to do  certain things  then we can immediately take  steps  that quickly relieve people  his attempt attempted demonstration also  promptly ended in his arrest  for more than 10 years uganda's  government has tried to stop street  protests before crowds can even gather  meanwhile the cost of living keeps  rising as it is in many countries but  about 40 percent of ugandans live on  less than two dollars a day and can't  afford to pay more  malcolm webb al jazeera
 

